Z||000040||pHoOl||03-04-2001||03:09 AM||||Well, to bring closure to all of this, I have absolute concrete proof that we americans, powered by the US Government never landed on the moon.  And you're all gonna hit your heads in frustration that you didn't realize it earlier.  You're all damned fools for thinking that we landed there.  There is absolutely no way that it could have happened.<P>Okay, i think i've hyped my answer up enough.  How is it that we could have landed on the moon thirty years ago, when we can't even count votes out of the same state that we launched the rocket from?  PROOF RIGHT THERE!!!!!<P><BR>PS. I think i remember hearing something about mysterious deaths of NASA employess, like one had a 500 page report that he was gonig to release, and suddenly a train hit him and the report that he had on his person was never found.  <P>There y'all go, glad i could answer all your questions.<P>Rev. phool<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000041||Wolfhound||03-04-2001||04:31 AM||||The Space and Rocket center in Huntsville has two Saturn 5 rockets on display. One is laid out horizontal on the museum yard with each stage disconected. The other stands vertical outside the museum. They are enormous.<P>I went down to watch the launch for the first moon landing. We were across the bay from the launch. (approx. 12 miles) It was large enough that you could see it clearly. It shook the ground at 12 miles. You could the sound wave comming across the marsh when the engines were started by the flight of the various water birds. It was a truly awesome sight. ||||reg||1
Z||000042||Black88GT||03-04-2001||02:26 PM||||I heard that like 20,000 NASA employees involved with the space thing just mysteriously disappeared, a couple got struck by mysterious lightning, and black helicopters allegedly came and took some of them away to some mysterious remote location that only the US Gov't knows about.  Hmmm seems a little fishy to me.<P>Ever wonder why meteorologists always talk about some big storm, then you see everyone run to the food store the next day.  When the day comes for the storm its either mysteriously not there or its not nearly as bad as they originally predicted?  I think thats a conspiracy too!!  SOMETHING IS FISHY<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||12
